{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.641,
   "text": "I close up an old bowling alley at the edge of town. Alone. Every night."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.341,
   "end": 13.544,
   "text": "The owner, Mr. Briggs, gave me one rule on my first shift."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.144,
   "end": 21.248,
   "text": "If the pins on lane twelve ever set themselves up after closing... don't bowl. Just kill the lights, and leave."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 22.048,
   "end": 24.8,
   "text": "For a whole month... nothing happened."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 25.4,
   "end": 30.392,
   "text": "Then one night, while I was mopping, the machine on lane twelve hummed to life."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 32.992,
   "end": 38.027,
   "text": "Ten white pins dropped into place... standing perfectly still in the dark."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 39.027,
   "end": 44.808,
   "text": "The little score screen above the lane blinked on. One player. The name just said... NEXT."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 46.208,
   "end": 49.557,
   "text": "I didn't bowl. I didn't look back. I just left."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 50.557,
   "end": 54.803,
   "text": "The next night, the screen had two players. NEXT... and Briggs."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 55.803,
   "end": 60.475,
   "text": "Mr. Briggs didn't come in the next morning. Or the morning after that."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 61.875,
   "end": 66.781,
   "text": "Tonight, when I unlocked the doors, the pins on twelve were already standing."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 67.781,
   "end": 70.128,
   "text": "The screen showed one player..."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 71.328,
   "end": 71.957,
   "text": "Me."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 73.557,
   "end": 79.232,
   "text": "And the ball return rumbled... and slowly rolled a ball up to my hand. Still warm."
  }
 ],
